    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Tuscan commune that grew rich on wool cloth and banking and ruled most of Tuscany by the fifteenth century.</li><li>Its gold florin, minted from 1252, became a standard coin of international trade across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>From 1434 the Medici steered the republic informally, and it was the birthplace of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#renaissance">Renaissance</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Florentine offices were filled by lot: names of eligible citizens were drawn from leather bags, and priors served for only two months.</p></aside>
    </section>

